Subject: [PATCH] omap3-beagle-ab4: run SGX functional clock at core/3 (110 MHz)

Early BeagleBoard (SGX530 rev 1.0.3): mainline leaves the SGX functional-clock
mux (CM_CLKSEL_SGX / sgx_mux_fck) parented to core/6 = 55 MHz, half the 110 MHz
the TI vendor kernel selected (core/3). At half clock, borderline GPU renders
take ~2x as long and overrun the PowerVR DDK's fixed 100 ms EVENT_OBJECT client
wait, producing the residual EVENT_OBJECT_WAIT timeouts/stalls. Reparent
sgx_mux_fck to core_d3_ck so sgx_fck runs at 110.67 MHz like the vendor kernel.

Verify at runtime: /sys/kernel/debug/clk/clk_summary shows sgx_fck = 110666666.

Applies to omap3-beagle-ab4.dts (the DTB this project ships); the clock labels
live in omap36xx-am35xx-omap3430es2plus-clocks.dtsi.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-beagle-ab4.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap3-beagle-ab4.dts
@@ -44,6 +44,18 @@
 	ti,no-idle;
 	timer@0 {
 		assigned-clocks = <&gpt2_fck>;
 		assigned-clock-parents = <&sys_ck>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Early BeagleBoard (SGX530 rev 1.0.3): mainline leaves the SGX functional-clock
+ * mux (CM_CLKSEL_SGX) parented to core/6 = 55 MHz, but the TI vendor kernel ran
+ * core/3 = 110 MHz. At half clock, borderline GPU renders overrun the DDK's fixed
+ * 100 ms EVENT_OBJECT wait and stall. Reparent to core_d3_ck (110.67 MHz).
+ */
+&sgx_mux_fck {
+	assigned-clocks = <&sgx_mux_fck>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&core_d3_ck>;
+};
